{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The adhesive-lined heat shrink tubing would help insulate and seal connections made with my crimp terminals, giving it a specific use alongside something I already bought.",
    "The heavy-duty hook-and-loop tape offers removable fastening for practical repairs, while the caliper would help me measure hoses and fittings before choosing parts."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Magnets, buffing compound and medical gloves do not address a task I currently have; being workshop supplies does not make them useful to me now.",
    "Ten tubes of super glue are not justified by my purchases of duct tape and vinyl cement, which served particular repairs. Likewise, hose clamps do not imply that I need plugs for threaded pipes."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair purchases seem to have been treated as broad interest in almost any tool or maintenance supply.",
    "Shared brands and general fastening uses seem to carry too much weight when the materials, strength and intended jobs differ."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "A concrete connection to an existing task matters: sealing crimp connections or measuring hose diameters is more compelling than simply offering another repair product.",
    "Product details affect my choice. I prefer the adhesive-lined tubing over the basic kit here, and the heavy-duty fastening tape seems more useful than lightweight strips; I would not choose both alternatives just because they are related."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my practical repair interests but sometimes confused a shared repair theme with a specific current need."
}"}
